Mark Healey wrote:
> I find that I wind up having lots of stuff that I have to leave in
> little piles under boulders before I find a good base camp spot.  When
> I do find one I usually have to make multiple trips to retrieve my
> goodies.
> 
> Pets will pick up stuff and drop it.  Is there a way to control it
> adequately so that a really strong one could carry my stash.

IIRC most pets never carry more than one unusable (by the pet) item, so 
bring your spare bag with you. Gelcubes may be an exception but they 
have the tendency to digest organic (even rotproof organic) material. 
Nymphs might be a good choice too since at least wild nymphs have no 
weight restrictions (soory, no wizmode here to check). Throwing your pet 
some meatballs (if it eats meat) can also train it to carry the stuff 
for longer time.

